      "message": "So a few notes on this hack which has [existed since at least 2015](https://codereview.chromium.org/1133443003/). Codecs have changed quite a bit since then, and the data needed here is almost available.\n\n    static constexpr const SkCodecs::Decoder decoders[] \u003d {\n        SkJpegDecoder::Decoder(),\n    };\n    auto codec \u003d SkCodec::MakeFromData(data, decoders);\n    codec-\u003egetICCProfile()-\u003ebuffer; // icc buffer pointer (if it exists)\n    codec-\u003egetICCProfile()-\u003esize; // icc buffer length\n    codec-\u003edimensions(); // jpegSize\n    codec-\u003egetOrigin(); // exifOrientation\n    codec-\u003egetEncodedInfo().color(); // jpegColorType, cannot get to the color?\n\nwith the missing bit being the encoded color info (which is here used to reject non-JFIF/DCT CMYK 4 channel JPEGs). Unfortunately, the `imageInfo` does not provide this needed bit of information and would need to be exposed to avoid this hack.",
